  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory follows Moracchini-Mazel in identifying Punta Cavallata, but the Barrington Atlas Map 48 incorrectly places the label much further west, at La Revellata.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A promontory on the north coast of Corsica mentioned by Ptolemy. Modern scholars identify it with the Punta Cavallata, which is located just west of the Gulf of Saint Florent.",
